{number: 168}
{title: Lord, I Want to Be a Christian}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Lord, I want to be a Christian
In my [Bb7] heart, in my [Eb] heart.
Lord, I want to be a [Ab] Christian in my [Eb] heart.
In my [Ab] heart, in my [Eb] heart,
Lord, I want to be a [Bb7] Christian in my [Eb] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Lord, I want to be more loving
In my [Bb7] heart, in my [Eb] heart.
Lord, I want to be more [Ab] loving in my [Eb] heart.
In my [Ab] heart, in my [Eb] heart,
Lord, I want to be more [Bb7] loving in my [Eb] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Lord, I want to be more holy
In my [Bb7] heart, in my [Eb] heart.
Lord, I want to be more [Ab] holy in my [Eb] heart.
In my [Ab] heart, in my [Eb] heart,
Lord, I want to be more [Bb7] holy in my [Eb] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Eb] Lord, I want to be like Jesus
In my [Bb7] heart, in my [Eb] heart.
Lord, I want to be like [Ab] Jesus in my [Eb] heart.
In my [Ab] heart, in my [Eb] heart,
Lord, I want to be like [Bb7] Jesus in my [Eb] heart.
{end_of_verse}
